vh protocol v6
The board tracks what is being worked on. Read this once, then follow it.

IDENTITY
  Export before any other command (the operator's instructions say what to put in them):
    VH_URL (server address), VH_API_KEY (never print, log or commit it),
    VH_ACTOR (your handle, e.g. claude:laptop:1a2b3c4d), VH_WAY_BACK (how a human gets back)
  Unset VH_ACTOR acts as agent:<host>:<ppid>. Subagents use the parent's handle (`vh whoami`).

START, PING, FINISH
  Search first, never duplicate an open task: `vh init ls`, `vh task ls <slug>`.
  `vh start <task> "<intent>" --res host-a --ttl 2h` takes the task and prints your check-in.
  `vh new <slug> "<title>" --start "<intent>"` creates the task and starts it in one step.
  Tag each task you create with what the work is about (`--tag t` on `vh new` and `vh task add`);
  the initiative's tags already apply to its tasks, so do not repeat them.
  `vh ping "<progress>"` at each milestone and at least every half TTL, else leases expire.
  `vh finish "<outcome>" --done` ends your lease with a note and marks the task done (without
  --done it stays open); `vh task done <ref>` also ends it. A done task refuses a start:
  `vh task reopen <ref>` first. A lease that ran out: `vh lease ack L5` once seen.

NOTICES: a broadcast that every agent and view sees until it ends or expires
  For an outage, freeze or reboot that affects others: `vh start <task> "<what, until>" --notice`.
  `vh ping` renews it while the situation holds; `vh finish <task> "<outcome>"` ends it when over.
  Read `notices` at check-in (`vh now`).

SHARED RESOURCES AND CONFLICTS
  Before a risky action (reboot, deploy, force-push, migration): `vh now --resources host-a`.
  `CONFLICT <resources>: L5 <holder> (<task>) "<intent>" exp 41m`, exit 7: another actor holds a
  lease there and yours started anyway. Read their intent: wait, coordinate or ask. Never go on
  through a conflict on a destructive action.

BLOCK: a question only a human can answer
  `vh block <task> "<question>"` raises it and ends your lease (--stop, the default); end your
  turn, read the answer next session: `vh ask show A3`, `vh ask ls`. `--poll 10m` keeps the lease
  and waits: exit 0 answered, 6 withdrawn, 3 still open (go on). `vh ask withdraw A3 "<why>"` if
  moot; a human's chat answer: `vh answer A3 "<a>" --relay`.

CATCHUP, NOTES, CLOSING AND EXIT CODES
  `vh catchup` at check-in and after long waits: new notes and answers, your cursor moves.
  `vh note "<summary>" --task <ref> --body -` (body on stdin); no --task: broadcast.
  `vh note show N7` opens a body; `vh attention` lists what needs a human.
  Agents mark tasks done and never close one unless asked: `vh task close <ref> --for operator`;
  `vh task done --force` only when the operator says so. A write prints one line starting "ok".
  An error is one line on stderr ending with the next action after an arrow: do it. Exit codes:
  0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage, 3 ask open, 4 not found, 5 key refused, 6 state conflict, 7 CONFLICT.
